<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Game Mode declaration for the Android Game Manager (API 33+).

    osu! is a rhythm game whose timing model REQUIRES that the OS does not silently
    cap our frame rate, force resolution downscaling, or otherwise interpose between
    our render output and the display compositor. Each of the four flags below opts
    OUT of the corresponding OS-level Game Mode intervention:

      supportsBatteryGameMode="false"
        Tell the OS we do not consent to "Battery" mode adjustments. With this set to
        true the system may cap us at 30Hz on AOSP / Pixel devices when battery saver
        is on — a 50% drop in input-to-photon update rate that destroys aim/timing.

      supportsPerformanceGameMode="false"
        We already pin big cores ourselves (see OboeBridge::start CPU affinity, and
        OsuGameAndroid.LoadComplete thread affinity), enable sustained performance
        mode at the right time, and request the highest seamless refresh rate. The
        OS Game Manager's "performance" branch overlaps with all of these and on some
        OEM ROMs (one-off Pixel 7 reports) flips the panel back to 60Hz to "save
        thermals", undoing our 120Hz selection.

      allowGameDownscaling="false"
        Refuse the OS-driven render-resolution downscaler. The framework already has
        a Scaling container (osu.Game.Configuration.OsuSetting.Scaling) the user
        can use; an OS-imposed second downscaler stacks on top and breaks
        hit-object pixel-perfect alignment.

      allowGameFpsOverride="false"
        Refuse the OS Game Mode FPS override (the AOSP "limit FPS" toggle). osu!
        gameplay timing is locked to the chosen FrameSync / refresh rate; an OS
        override silently halves frame rate and shifts perceived latency.
-->
<game-mode-config xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:supportsBatteryGameMode="false"
    android:supportsPerformanceGameMode="false"
    android:allowGameDownscaling="false"
    android:allowGameFpsOverride="false" />
